1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,040
If I haven't had the privilege of meeting you, my name is Ryan, and I have the privilege

2
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:28,000
of being one of the pastors here, and we are four weeks into a brand new series that's

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,800
going to be on and off for—wow, it's bright up here, Sean.

4
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,560
You're going to be in for a treat here.

5
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,100
This is great.

6
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:40,540
That's going to go on and off for the next three-ish years, and the goal of it is to help

7
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,440
us grow in our relationship with Jesus.

8
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:47,760
All of the Bible is about a God who pursues us, who wants a relationship with us, and the

9
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:50,820
goal of that relationship is that we be conformed to the image of Jesus.

10
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:56,800
So this series pulls nine practices from the life and teachings of Jesus, all aimed at helping

11
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,740
us grow in that relationship with God.

12
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:00,460
Our first practice is prayer.

13
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:07,340
So far, we've talked about—hold on, I've got it—talking to God, talking with God.

14
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:10,380
And this week, we're going to talk about listening to God.

15
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:15,920
And I have the distinct honor and privilege of introducing a guest speaker this morning,

16
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,020
a good friend of mine by the name of Pastor Sean Wilson.

17
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:24,260
Him and his wife, Stephanie, and their son, Judah, have been pastors in our area for a while.

18
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:29,360
I got to meet him when we were kind of launching a prayer group for pastors in the area.

19
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,560
Sean was like the first person that I reached out to.

20
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:36,940
And for those of you that know the principle and Scripture of a person of peace, I found

21
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:40,900
Sean to be a person of peace when it comes to pastors getting together to pray.

22
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,480
He was eager and excited and hosted our first gathering.

23
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:48,960
And ever since then, Sean and I have been growing in a friendship, I think.

24
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,860
I'll let him talk about it.

25
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:58,120
And recently, Sean found himself in a similar spot as to me where he became the lead pastor,

26
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:00,400
not necessarily intending to do so.

27
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:04,420
And recently, they decided to kind of take a break from that ministry.

28
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:06,520
You guys have probably heard of a fresh church in our area.

29
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:12,120
And Sean's just been kind of staying connected in our community and blessing our community

30
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:14,220
with his desire to see the kingdom built.

31
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:17,240
And him and Stephanie are praying about what God might have next.

32
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:23,960
The reason I invited Sean is because this message on listening prayer has some elements

33
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:26,880
of what some of us in the room would call charismatic.

34
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:29,240
Anybody excited about that in the room?

35
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:31,260
If you're charismatic in the room, let me hear it.

36
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:35,980
Okay, we got one loud and proud charismatic in the room.

37
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:39,160
No, I know there's more of you than that.

38
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:43,460
Hey, one of our core values at our church is we unite for the sake of the gospel.

39
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:48,380
And so there are people in this room that have differing views on the gifts of the spirit

40
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:50,180
and how they work in the body of Christ.

41
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:54,920
And we just say here at Canvas, we preach the Bible and we unite for the sake of the gospel.

42
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:57,980
The gifts of the spirit is a secondary issue.

43
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:00,840
So I don't know where you fall on these issues.

44
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:06,260
But what I do know is that there's somebody smarter than you who loves Jesus who disagrees with you.

45
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:10,920
So that's my litmus test for uniting for the sake of the gospel.

46
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:14,060
So if there's somebody smarter than you who loves Jesus that disagrees,

47
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:17,560
we could probably unite for the sake of the gospel.

48
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:22,300
So rather than being the Baptist kid coming up here telling you how to listen to the Holy Spirit,

49
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:25,400
I decided to invite my charismatic friend, Sean Wilson.

50
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,880
So you guys can give it up for Sean.

51
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:34,480
Brother, we're excited to hear what the Lord has laid on your heart for us.

52
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:35,640
Yeah.

53
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:36,640
Awesome.

54
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:37,340
Is this thing on?

55
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:38,060
Hello.

56
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:40,120
Is everyone glad to be here this morning?

57
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,260
Awesome.

58
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,000
Hey, can we give it up for your pastors?

59
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:43,900
Come on.

60
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:44,760
Give it up for your leaders.

61
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:46,100
Man, they're awesome.

62
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:49,380
Show them honor where honor is due.

63
00:03:49,380 --> 00:03:51,900
But man, I'm excited to be here this morning.

64
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,020
Thank you for the invitation.

65
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:55,240
Thank you for the honor to be here.

66
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,400
What a heck of an introduction.

67
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,560
I don't know if I can beat that.

68
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:01,400
But yeah, so my name is Sean.

69
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:06,580
My wife and I, we used to pastor a church called the Fresh Church right here in Winchester.

70
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,460
We love this city.

71
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:08,240
We love Jesus.

72
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:13,520
We love to see people come to know the presence of God in such a real and tangible way.

73
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:17,320
We love when people get to experience the love of God in such a real and tangible way.

74
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:19,660
And so that's really ultimately our heart.

75
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:24,440
So however we can do that, whether it's through a vocational ministry or not, we're just going

76
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:25,100
to see it happen.

77
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:28,280
And I believe God's got a big plan for Winchester, don't you?

78
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:29,420
Yeah.

79
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:30,660
So awesome.

80
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,500
We love Jesus and we love his word.

81
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:37,060
And so, you know, I'm honored to have the privilege to preach it today.

82
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:38,380
So let's jump right in.

83
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:41,120
We're talking about listening to God.

84
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:44,480
We're going to jump right into John chapter 10.

85
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,360
Who's got a paper Bible in the room?

86
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:46,860
Let me see him.

87
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:47,760
Hold him loud and proud.

88
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:49,100
Okay, a few of us.

89
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:51,300
The rest of you can scroll to John chapter 10.

90
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:58,540
While you guys are getting there, let me give you just a little bit of background on

91
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:01,240
kind of what we're talking about today.

92
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:04,040
So Ryan kind of introduced the whole thing.

93
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:08,640
You know, you guys have been in a series called Practicing the Way and this segment here is

94
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,360
on prayer.

95
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:12,700
You've already talked about talking to God and talking with God.

96
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:18,700
Today, I want to talk to us about hearing the voice of God, hearing the voice of God.

97
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:23,380
I want to talk about what it looks like to hear the voice of God in your life and how

98
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,520
we can do that through prayer.

99
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:30,840
And so in John chapter 10, we jump right in, we jump right into Jesus criticizing the Pharisees

100
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,780
as he often does.

101
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:38,240
They've got a lot of messed up stuff, but he's criticizing them because the Pharisees

102
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,940
do not care about the people that they lead.

103
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:41,280
They don't care about the people they lead.

104
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:42,400
And Jesus does.

105
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:46,520
And he's coming to tell us how much of a better leader that he can be.

106
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:49,280
And so right here in John chapter 10, we'll start in verse one.

107
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,060
We'll go all the way to 14.

108
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:53,620
And if you don't have a Bible, it'll be up on the screen, I believe.

109
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:54,240
Awesome.

110
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:54,640
Awesome.

111
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:55,700
It says this.

112
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:57,040
I tell you the truth.

113
00:05:57,040 --> 00:06:02,620
Anyone who sneaks over the wall of a sheepfold rather than going through the gate must surely

114
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,360
be a thief and a robber.

115
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:08,160
But the one who enters through the gate is the shepherd of the sheep.

116
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:13,560
The gatekeeper opens the sheep for him and the sheep recognize his voice and come to him.

117
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:16,700
He calls his own sheep by name and he leads them out.

118
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:21,980
After he's gathered his own flock, he walks ahead of them and they follow him because they

119
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:23,800
know his voice.

120
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,280
They won't follow a stranger.

121
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:27,960
They would run from his voice because they don't know his voice.

122
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:31,260
Sorry, they will run from him because they don't know his voice.

123
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:34,780
Those who heard Jesus use this illustration didn't understand what he meant.

124
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:35,840
So he explained it to them.

125
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:36,680
I tell you the truth.

126
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,420
I am the gate for the sheep.

127
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:43,740
All who come before me were thieves and robbers, but the true sheep did not listen to them.

128
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,260
Yes, I am the gate.

129
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:48,420
Those who come in through me will be saved.

130
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:52,120
They will come and go freely and will find good pastures.

131
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:55,540
The thief's purpose is to steal, kill, and destroy.

132
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:59,480
But my purpose is to give them a rich and a satisfying life.

133
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,740
Some translations say an abundant life.

134
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:02,280
That's so good.

135
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:05,240
Verse 11 says, I am the good shepherd.

136
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:09,560
The good shepherd sacrifices his life for the sheep.

137
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:12,060
A hired hand will run when he sees a wolf coming.

138
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:15,180
He will abandon the sheep because they do not belong to him.

139
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,440
And he isn't their shepherd.

140
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,800
And so the wolf attacks them and scatters the flock.

141
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:23,320
The hired hand runs away because he's working only for the money and doesn't really care about the sheep.

142
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,980
But I am the good shepherd.

143
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:29,100
I know my own sheep and they know me.

144
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:29,940
Do me a favor.

145
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:31,660
Turn to your neighbor and say, you're a sheep.

146
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:32,960
You're a sheep.

147
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:34,960
Turn to your other neighbor and say, bah.

148
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,760
Sounds like a good pasture in here.

149
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:41,660
Oh, man.

150
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:53,200
We are sheep and we have a good shepherd who wants to lead us and he wants to guide us into a rich and a satisfying or an abundant life that he has for us.

151
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:58,200
And so I want to talk to us about the importance of hearing God's voice in our lives.

152
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:05,820
And I would argue that this is probably one of the most important things that we can learn to do as Christians, to hear God's voice.

153
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:06,040
Why?

154
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:12,620
Because I believe that hearing God's voice is the pathway to the rich and satisfying and abundant life that Jesus offers.

155
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:15,120
So let's pray and open this up this morning.

156
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:17,020
Lord, thank you for your presence.

157
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:18,960
Thank you for your spirit that is here.

158
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:26,600
Lord, I just pray that you would begin to stir something up in us today as we study your word and as we receive from you.

159
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,880
Lord, I just pray you'd speak to us this morning.

160
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:32,580
Let our hearts know what we need to know and let our ears hear what we need to hear.

161
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:37,200
Lord, I pray you'd bless our meeting this morning and just have your way in this place.

162
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:41,920
In Jesus' mighty name, all the church said, amen and amen and amen.

163
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:44,160
Anyone here like to vacation?

164
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,860
I know it's early in the year.

165
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:49,940
Does anyone need a vacation 2024 already?

166
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:50,860
Yeah, okay.

167
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:51,700
I thought so.

168
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:55,800
Hey, you want to know my least favorite thing about vacationing?

169
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,840
Driving, driving.

170
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:00,940
And it's not, I actually don't mind driving all that much.

171
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:07,340
It's the stuff that comes along with the driving that really just sucks the fun out of the whole trip.

172
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:10,420
Things like, you know, I love my wife, but she's got a squirrel bladder.

173
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:13,540
She's got to pee every, you know, every couple miles, you know.

174
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:15,400
And it's like, oh my gosh, we got to stop again.

175
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:17,740
Or my son, he gets hungry all the time.

176
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:19,440
Or he poops in the car seat.

177
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,140
That's real fun, you know.

178
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:24,220
Or people, oh, this drives me nuts.

179
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:29,360
People that don't realize that the left lane of the interstate is for passing, not for driving.

180
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:29,640
Amen?

181
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:32,700
It's for passing, not for cruising.

182
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,360
I'll be 29 this year.

183
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,040
Yeah, scary.

184
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:40,800
And now there's this weird back pain that I get after about two hours.

185
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:43,220
And it just appears and comes and never leaves.

186
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,980
So I don't know what that's all about, but that's fun.

187
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:50,580
And why is it that it's always the drive home that is longer than the drive there, you know?

188
00:09:50,580 --> 00:09:57,080
I think when I think of vacation, I kind of dread it a little bit just because I'm like, ugh, we have to endure all of that.

189
00:09:57,080 --> 00:10:02,460
And it never fails that I end up being the only one awake about an hour and 45 minutes into the trip.

190
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:05,060
My son's the first to go immediately.

191
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:07,900
As soon as we leave the driveway, you know, he's out.

192
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:10,880
My wife, she can hang on for a little bit longer.

193
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:14,880
But I notice Stephanie, as she drifts off, you know, the conversations get shorter.

194
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:20,300
See her head kind of bob a little bit as she's, you know, trying to fall asleep.

195
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:26,080
And the main reason I know that she's falling asleep is because she doesn't criticize how fast I'm going.

196
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:28,220
So I'm able to tell.

197
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,200
She's not paying attention.

198
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,380
She's dozing off, okay?

199
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:33,680
And it's so weird how you can be totally awake and alert.

200
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:37,180
And then when everybody falls asleep, you're like, hmm, I can't keep my eyes open, right?

201
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:40,780
It's a good thing I have a good friend that travels with us all the time.

202
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:43,820
She never falls asleep, and she always tells me everything I need to know.

203
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:46,100
Her name is Siri, and she's wonderful.

204
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:47,340
She comes with us on every trip.

205
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:51,040
And she knows how fast I'm going, and she doesn't tell me to slow down.

206
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,420
She just puts it passive-aggressively in the bottom left corner.

207
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:54,640
I love her.

208
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:55,380
She's awesome.

209
00:10:55,380 --> 00:11:00,700
But Siri, Siri will tell you everything you need to know the moment you need to know it.

210
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:01,200
It's awesome.

211
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:04,020
And does anybody else have their Siri in an Australian voice?

212
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:06,320
Okay, just a few of us.

213
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:09,460
You know, she says things like, hey, you've made a wrong tune.

214
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,380
You've got to turn around.

215
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:12,640
You know, I'm going to recalculate, or whatever.

216
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:14,860
Or, hey, there's an accident in six miles.

217
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:17,060
You want to take an alternate route and save 14 minutes?

218
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:18,640
It's like, oh, this is awesome.

219
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:22,680
But my favorite that I love whenever she says this, your destination's on the right.

220
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:24,400
It's like, oh, praise God we're here.

221
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,500
Right?

222
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:28,200
Remember what we used to do without Siri?

223
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,220
We had, like, MapQuest.

224
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:30,160
Any MapQuesters?

225
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:31,780
All right, I'm going to really test your age.

226
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:32,940
Who had an atlas growing up?

227
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:34,560
Oh, okay.

228
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,100
We have a nice demographic here.

229
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:36,420
That's good.

230
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:36,740
That's good.

231
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,740
Imagine still needing to do that.

232
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:42,060
Can you imagine if we had to read atlases today?

233
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:42,820
We wouldn't get anywhere.

234
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:46,200
You know, we still miss turns, even with voice navigation, right?

235
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:51,240
And now we just get the sweet Australian voice to come and travel with us everywhere that we go

236
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:57,440
and help us navigate through what used to be the most stressful part of vacation and traveling.

237
00:11:57,440 --> 00:12:00,680
And, you know, don't you kind of wish life was like that a little bit?

238
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:07,640
Don't you wish, like, you had someone to tell you and help navigate you through the stressful times of life?

