00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:48,260
And I've got some good news for us today to share with you.

270
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:52,740
So if you're taking notes, write this down, it's this, God wants to speak to you.

271
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:57,100
God wants to, he doesn't have to, he doesn't need to.

272
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:58,600
He wants to speak to you.

273
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,900
He wants to speak to you.

274
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:00,120
Why?

275
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,640
Because he loves you.

276
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:05,900
He's a relational God and he wants the best for you.

277
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:07,720
He wants to guide you through this life.

278
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:13,500
You see, Jesus died on the cross for our sin, a sin debt that we could not pay on our own.

279
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:15,480
He took the cross that we owe.

280
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:18,280
He paid for the sin on the cross that we deserve.

281
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:26,720
And after that, he ascended, he went into heaven and he gave us his Holy Spirit to live in us, not near us, but in us.

282
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:27,180
Okay?

283
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:31,260
If you're a Christian today, you have the presence of God living in you.

284
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,440
You're a presence carrier.

285
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:35,580
Everywhere that you go, God goes with you.

286
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:38,080
You're a presence carrier.

287
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:40,800
You're a host of the Holy Ghost, if you will.

288
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:44,340
And Jesus describes the Holy Spirit like this.

289
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:46,360
In John 14, he says, he's an advocate.

290
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,560
He's a comforter.

291
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:48,640
He's an encourager.

292
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:49,620
He's a counselor.

293
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:50,520
He's a helper.

294
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:54,800
And then he says that the Holy Spirit leads us into all truth.

295
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,240
He's a leader.

296
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,760
He's a guide.

297
00:14:57,760 --> 00:15:03,140
And how good would a guide really be if he never communicated with us?

298
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:10,500
How good would Siri really be if she never said anything, if she let you miss the turn, right?

299
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:17,160
How good would your boss really be if they never told you how to do your job properly, right?

300
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:21,280
Good guides give instruction, direction, and correction.

301
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:28,000
And I love that Jesus calls himself the good shepherd because that's exactly what a shepherd does, right?

302
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,480
Look at this in our passage in John 10, verse 3.

303
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:34,060
He says, the gatekeeper opens the gate for him, and the sheep recognize his voice and come to him.

304
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:37,620
He calls his own sheep by name and what?

305
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:38,780
Leads them out.

306
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:40,020
He leads them out.

307
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:45,260
Isaiah, in the Old Testament, prophesies about a better time when Jesus would come and give us the Holy Spirit.

308
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:47,780
And he says this in Isaiah 30, verse 21.

309
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,080
He says, your own ears will hear him.

310
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:55,340
Right behind you, a voice will say, this is the way you should go, whether to the right or to the left.

311
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:58,840
It's clear that God wants to speak to his people.

312
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:03,740
He wants to lead you through this life, to give you a life with purpose.

313
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:05,860
He wants to be actively involved.

314
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:10,800
And here's some good news today if you're feeling down, but every person has the ability to hear God.

315
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:15,420
Every person has the ability to hear the voice of God.

316
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:17,920
It doesn't take a theology degree to hear the voice of God.

317
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:18,440
Praise God.

318
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:24,160
It doesn't take, you know, serving on the prayer team for five years to hear the voice of God.

319
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:28,480
You don't need a special spiritual gift to hear the voice of God.

320
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,280
All it takes is being his child.

321
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,560
He's a good father.

322
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:36,900
He's a good leader, and he wants to speak to us.

323
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:40,060
And you might sit there and be like, okay, that's wonderful.

324
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:40,800
Good to know.

325
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,720
Why doesn't he speak to me?

326
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,820
Let's just be real in the house, right?

327
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:46,620
Can we be real in church today?

328
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:49,340
Come on, I've prayed many, many prayers.

329
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:53,580
There have been many times in my prayer life where I'm like, God, please give me an answer to this.

330
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,040
God, please tell me what I need to do.

331
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:55,940
God, please speak to me.

332
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:58,260
And it seems like I didn't pray loud enough.

333
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:00,500
It seems like I didn't pray passionately enough.

334
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:03,620
It seems like I, you know, it seems like I didn't pray hard enough, whatever.

335
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:06,260
And, you know, surely I'm not the only one.

336
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:11,640
And we can ask ourselves, why, if God is speaking to everybody else, why is he not speaking to me?

337
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:13,680
Why is he not speaking to me?

338
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:17,940
And perhaps the issue isn't God not speaking.

339
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:22,420
Perhaps the issue is us not listening.

340
00:17:22,420 --> 00:17:27,400
Parents with kids with ADHD, you know exactly what I'm talking about.

341
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:31,420
Come on, you speak, but they do not hear.

342
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:32,480
You're speaking to the void.

343
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:36,460
My mom and my wife know this really well.

344
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,840
I'm not accusing us of having spiritual ADHD.

345
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:41,520
Just let me clarify.

346
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:46,580
But it's clear, excuse me, it's clear in the Scriptures that God speaks, yes?

347
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:49,360
And so the issue is not on God's end.

348
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,620
It's not God's depravity.

349
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:51,820
It's not God's problem.

350
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:54,680
Look at what the author of Hebrews says about this in Hebrews 12, 25.

351
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:55,400
He says,

352
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:56,900
Be careful that you, what?

353
00:17:56,900 --> 00:18:00,940
Do not refuse to listen to the one who is speaking.

354
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:03,000
I'm going to read it again, just in case you didn't hear it.

355
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:09,600
Be careful that you do not refuse to listen to the one who is speaking.

356
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:11,280
Do not refuse.

357
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:16,060
Do not be unwilling to listen to the one, to the God who is speaking.

358
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:18,020
Which tells us this, if you're taking notes, write this down.

359
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:20,540
That listening requires intention.

360
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:23,960
Listening requires intention.

361
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:25,260
Intention.

362
00:18:25,260 --> 00:18:27,540
We have to be intentional about hearing God.

363
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,520
We have to be intentional about listening to God.

364
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:33,740
We have to be in tune with the Lord to be aware of what he is speaking to you.

365
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:34,960
Think of it like a radio.

366
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:39,080
There's all sorts of different radio stations that are broadcasting different radio waves.

367
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:40,940
You can't listen to all of them at the same time.

368
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:41,600
What do you have to do?

369
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:45,280
You have to tune the radio to the proper frequency to hear the station.

370
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:47,860
Just because you're not tuned in doesn't mean the radio is not playing.

371
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,620
You have to be tuned in to the proper frequency.

372
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:55,660
We have to be tuned in to what the Lord is saying and be intentional about hearing him.

373
00:18:55,660 --> 00:19:01,200
And if you aren't listening for the Lord's voice, hate to break it to you, you're probably not going to hear it.

374
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,840
Right?

375
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:10,600
And I think there's generally, not entirely, but generally two reasons that we struggle to hear the voice of God.

376
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:17,280
Number one is this, is that part of the reason we struggle to hear God's voice is simply because we just don't take time to listen.

377
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:19,020
Right?

378
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:21,460
We don't give him time to speak to us.

379
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:24,720
How often do we just pray a prayer just to get it over with?

380
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:30,480
I think, Pastor Ryan, you talked about this a couple weeks ago about prayer sometimes being a chore or a duty.

381
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:30,780
Right?

382
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:36,280
You know, sometimes we just pray so quickly just to get out of the way.

383
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,660
You know, we wake up early in the morning.

384
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:38,520
We're like, okay, I'm early.

385
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:41,200
I'm spiritual because you got to pray in the morning to be more spiritual.

386
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,000
You know?

387
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:46,060
Or like the psalmist said, you know, I wake up in the morning and I pray.

